Z||000014||Songman||08-23-2001||03:59 PM||||I have a cricket and a Sprint...<P>The Cricket is advertised at $29.99 per month but by the time you add caller ID and voice mail, plus taxes it comes out to $40.<P>It is only good in your one area, and in some cases not even good then. I live 25 miles outside of Nashville and my Cricket won't work at my house. And on Music Row, right downtown Nashville, hardly any cell phones work. Don't know what that is about.<P>Anyway, from my understanding, you can get a plan that allows you to make long distance calls from your Cricket but it is something outrageous like 16 cents per minute or something. I used to just go down to this market and buy the 2 cent per minute calling cards. Of course, now with my Sprint phone with free long distance I don't have to worry about it...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
