Z||000057||Mach10||08-25-2001||09:09 PM||||That's good. You just seem to brush it off lightly by your posts. Remember, it's not un-professional to ask someone to leave, please.<P>The same way when the stupid *******  on the other end of the phone starts ranting and cursing, I can tell him that there is no reason to use that kind of language, and to call back when he's called down, please. Thank You for Calling ********@home. Goodbye *click*<P>Don't feel that you can't say anything "because they are a customer." Some people WILL take advantage of this. You just have to keep it professional. I'd talk to the boss, and let him/her know that you are BEING SEXUALLY HARRASSED. That usually makes the "lawsuit bells" go off in people's heads, and look for ways to improve things. At least, that's how it works up here. I remember from somewhere that your father owns/part owns the chain? That doesn't mean that you don't have access to the same safe, comfortable work environment. <BR>||||reg||14
