Z||000098||Formula88||08-31-2001||03:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>I haven't touched my Fiero in over a week, except I started it to make sure it would for the meeting Sunday. Hmmm oh well.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Why don't you drive your Fiero more?  I've got my 99 Grand Am as my daily driver (yeah, right) but about the only time I drive it is when the Fiero's out of commission or I need the extra room.  When I go outside and notice the rust on the brake rotors, I know it's time to drive the GA again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000099||FieroLisa||08-31-2001||04:03 PM||||The reason I don't drive the Fiero much is cause I sit in a mall all day. You couldn't pay me to park my Fiero at the mall and let people slam their doors into it and drive into it, etc.  My tracer got beat all to h#ll in my school's parking lot.<P>Hmm I drove the Prelude today, I think it's kinda fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>TODAY SUCKS. 3.5 hours and I've had about 3 people walk in here- none to buy phones, just to ask where another store is, or to buy accessories. I've made $6 in accessory commission...umm woo hoo.||||reg||1
Z||000100||Formula88||08-31-2001||04:43 PM||||Ok, I agree completely with that.  My GA has dings from parking it at work - and I don't even work at the mall, so it's the same all over.  <P>Asking directions, huh?  'Hi, my name is Lisa.  Down towards the far end of the mall and to the left is where you can go f*ck yourself.'   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  'Unless, of course, you'd like to buy a phone.'<P>I used to get that all the time when I worked a the Colony Theater in Raleigh (then call the Terrace Twin).  People would walk up to the box office and ask me where the OTHER theatre was on Six Forks Rd.  (Our competition, no less).  Since it was off the main road a bit, you won't know where it is if you don't know where you're going.  So I'd tell 'em to just head North on Six Forks Rd. until you see it on the left.  They'd drive into Falls Lake before they'd ever see that theatre from the road!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If you can see a pay phone from your store - you could always try one of my favorite bits.  Get the phone number and call the pay phone when someone is about to walk by it.  When they answer, just say in a deep, threatening voice, "Don't turn around."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Invariably, they'll turn around - then you shout, "I told you not to turn around!" and whatever else you find amusing.  It works best on young teenagers with their girlfriends, cuz it makes 'em look stupid in front of her.  That, or I've just become a bitter old man...  Ah, well.  The world's goin' to hell, and I'm watchin' the parade!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000101||FieroLisa||08-31-2001||06:15 PM||||wow, today takes the cake as being the worst, slowest day ever. NO sales, 5 accessories in all, only 2 of which are mine.  Jiminy christmas... and it's raining, uggggg, i feel like crap... sorry for the pity party, but it's definitely one of those days  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000102||Old Lar||08-31-2001||06:40 PM||||You need to stay at work...$210 spent on your day off, how long does it take to make that much in commissions?<P>I drove my 88 Fiero to the grocery store yesterday, the first time since coming back from Denver Pa.<P>I haven't driven my 87 in several weeks, since going to the upholstry shop for a new headliner.<P>I'd like to go to the Fierorama, but I'm stocking up $$ to pay for all the Fiero trips I've taken this year.  Only a couple of road trips left for 2001.  I'm getting bummed out.<P>Too busy at work to get board.||||reg||1
Z||000103||Formula88||08-31-2001||06:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>wow, today takes the cake as being the worst, slowest day ever. NO sales, 5 accessories in all, only 2 of which are mine.  Jiminy christmas... and it's raining, uggggg, i feel like crap... sorry for the pity party, but it's definitely one of those days   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>And not even a casual booty comment to liven things up, huh?  Oh, well.  Look at it this way.  I've heard of lots of Post Office employees going Postal, but have you ever heard of someone going Cellular on somebody?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000104||artherd||08-31-2001||07:40 PM||||I like big butts and I cannot lie!!!  &lt;everybody now!&gt;  <P>Seriously Lisa, I'm surprised you put up with that crap, though not very (it seems to happen so much, I'd just eventually ignore it myself.) It'd be almost flattering if it weren't coming from what must be Stacy's extended and insane family  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I've ridden a horse once or twice, *definately* a sport, and a team one at that!<P>Hey, wait, I may be on  to something here, maybe you're supposed to wear clothes to work?  Nah, that'd be no fun, your way's better!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>9 phones sold today so far woo hoo!!<P>But of course, the scary guy problem:  middle aged black guy comes in and starts talkin like he wants to buy a phone. So I talk to him, then walk around the counter to show him the phones. When I walk back to behind the counter to the computer he says "Now you better stay behind that counter there. You a real good sales lady, but stay behind it" I asked him why like 3 times and finally he was like "Well from behind that counter your a petite lady but when you walked around that derriere surprised me."  SO I'm not sure if my ghetto booty is good or bad. He then asked me if I played any sports since I look "athletic" I told him I rode horses and he was trying to tell me it wasn't a sport- whatever!!! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
